><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Cheung</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Measuring Personality and values across cultures: imported versus indigenous measures</article-title><source>Online Readings in Psychology and Culture</source><volume>6</volume><issue>5</issue></element-citation></ref><ref id="b11-copd-2-313"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cleophas</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Hornstra</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>van Hoogstraten</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Homocysteine, a risk factor for coronary artery disease or not? A meta-analysis</article-title><source>Am J Cardiol</source><volume>86</volume><issue>9</issue><fpage>1005</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><fpage>A8</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11053715</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="b12-copd-2-313"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cockburn</surname><given-names>BN</given-names></name><name><surname>Bermano</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Boodram</surname><given-names>LL</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Gene symbol: IPF1. Disease: MODY 4</article-title><source>Hum Genet</source><volume>116</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>538</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15991313</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="b13-copd-2-313"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Crapo</surname><given-names>Ro</given-names></name><name><surname>Morris</surname><given-names>AH</given-names></name><name><surname>Gardnar</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name></person-group><year>1981</year><article-title>Reference spirometric values using techniques and equipment that meets ATS recommendations</article-title><source>Am Rev Respir Dis</source><volume>123</volume><fpage>654</fpage><lpage>59</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7271064</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="b14-copd-2-313"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dahl</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Vestbo</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Lange</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Dahl C-reactive Protein is a Strong Predictor of Prognosis in COPD</article-title><source>Am J Respir Crit Care Med</source><volume>175</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>250</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17053205</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="b15-copd-2-313"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Danesh</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Collins</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Appleby</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Direct proinflammatory effects of fibrinogen, C-rective protein, albumin or leukocyte count with coronary heart disease: meta-analyses of prospective studies</article-title><source>JAMA</source><volume>279</volume><fpage>2165</fpage><lpage>68</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="b16-copd-2-313"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Davison</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Translation of fixed-response questionnaires for health research with aboriginal people: a discussion of methods</article-title><source>Pimatsiwin: A Journal of Aboriginal and Indigenous Community Health</source><volume>2</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>97</fpage><lpage>114</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="b17-copd-2-313"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Durga</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>van Tits</surname><given-names>LJH</given-names></name><name><surname>Schouten</surname><given-names>EG</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Effect of lowering of homocysteine levels on inflammatory markers: a randomized controlled trial</article-title><source>Arch Intern Med</source><volume>165</volume><fpage>1388</fpage><lpage>94</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15983288</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="b18-copd-2-313"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fabiosa</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Mohanty</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>Conceptual Framework and Software Documentation. Jamaica Technical Manual</article-title><source>CARD Technical Report</source>97&#x02013;TR 33.</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b19-copd-2-313"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gan</surname><given-names>WQ</given-names></name><name><surname>Man</surname><given-names>SFP</given-names></name><name><surname>Senthilselvan</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Association between chronic obstructive pulmonary disease and systemic inflammation: a systematic review and a meta-analysis</article-title><source>Thorax</source><volume>59</volume><fpage>574</fpage><lpage>80</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15223864</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="b20-copd-2-313"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Goyette</surname><given-names>P</given-names>